          "caption": "This beautiful cove was the royal canoe landing, for use only by the ali'i. The area was forbidden to all commoners, and anyone entering it would be violating sacred law (kapu) and could be killed on the spot. There is a wooden marker in the cove warning people of the kapu. Wooden images (ki'i) also stand watch over the cove. The Keone'ele Cove is an excellent place for snorkeling. Sea turtles come to swim in the clear water and sun themselves on the beach\nRoyal Grounds, Pu'uhonua o Honaunau National Historic Park, Honaunau, Big Island, Hawaii  \n\nSource:  Nature.nps.gov",
